ry\\\":556,\\\"deltaFromPriorBaseline\\\":3},\\\"gatesRun\\\":[{\\\"command\\\":\\\"corepack pnpm run green-verify\\\",\\\"result\\\":\\\"pass\\\"},{\\\"command\\\":\\\"corepack pnpm run verify-all\\\",\\\"result\\\":\\\"pass\\\"}],\\\"selfReview\\\":{\\\"passesRun\\\":3,\\\"findingsFixed\\\":[\\\"Confirmed AC-1.1 through AC-1.3 are covered in behavior by stripping shell ownership fields, preserving process-local current-material projection, and enabling referenced-artifact review entry without ownership transfer.\\\",\\\"Validated the in-scope test-plan obligations with added server coverage for shell summary shape, current-material reference behavior, and cross-process referenced review access.\\\",\\\"Caught and fixed the temporary integration regression from a too-narrow current-ref-only reviewability rule, then re-ran both story and epic gates successfully.\\\"],\\\"findingsSurfaced\\\":[\\\"Legacy artifact-row ownership hints still exist in some internal durable/test seams as compatibility residue; this story stops relying on them in the affected read paths, but Story 2 remains the write-path cleanup point.\\\",\\\"Review eligibility now intentionally unions current refs with produced-artifact visibility to preserve existing shipped behavior during this chunk; a later epic/story can narrow or replace that compatibility path once package-context and full review-context alignment land.\\\"]},\\\"openQuestions\\\":[],\\\"specDeviations\\\":[],\\\"recommendedNextStep\\\":\\\"Proceed to verification with focused checks on cross-process artifact reference behavior in the project shell, process materials, and review entry paths, then carry the deferred write-path and compatibility cleanup into Story 2 and later review-context alignment work.\\\"}\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/artifacts/01-project-artifact-association-without-process-ownership/002-self-review-pass-1.json:1:{\\\"resultId\\\":\\\"7ce2d942-da23-454f-9c60-7d